# std/agent-spawn (design/caos-expr.md): an entry for an OPERATION OF THE STEP. `@op` says llm-step
# does the work in process (it owns the session's own records and the call's
# lifecycle), so this entry exists to give the operation a path, a help and a place in
# `tool_help`/`run_tool`. The image it curries is never run.
HELP=<<END
Start a focused coding agent in a durable child session. The child receives an isolated copy of the session files and source trees (excluding protocol metadata) and can be joined with agent-wait, then selected content can be applied with agent-harvest. Returns the child id.
@param prompt A self-contained task with the desired output and constraints.
@param {array} [paths] Session-relative paths to copy. Omit for all content. Select code references as whole source trees. Protocol metadata is always excluded.
@op agent-spawn
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --help=$HELP
